Description: EDITION ONLY: hand the stereo layer the views at their own resolution
 .
 The layer took the views from extractView(), which restores a half
 view to the size of a view with the filter stereoScaling names (Lanczos
 by default), and the compositor then resized the restored views again
 to the item: two resizes of a half top-and-bottom or side by side
 video, the first of them on the CPU.
 .
 storedView() copies each view at the resolution the frame carries it,
 never scaled: the half of a side by side or top and bottom frame, half
 or full, the even or odd rows or columns of an interleaved one, the
 row's own checkers of a checkerboard, the whole frame of a frame
 sequence. The layer hands those over (a half top-and-bottom 1920x1080
 video as one 3840x540 buffer), and its viewport, which has the shape of
 a view, gives the compositor the one resize. stereoScaling stays for a
 view shown flat in the scene graph.
